{
  "title": "1st Day of Zilhajj",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Introduction\nA number of devotional acts may be practiced on this blessed day:\nFirst: It is recommended to observe fasting on this day, for its reward is equal to the reward of eighty months worship.\nSecond: It is recommended to offer Salat Faatemah. According to Shaykh al-Tusi, this prayer consists of four units each couple of which are offered separately. At each unit, Surah al-Faatehah is recited once and Surah al-Tawheed repeated fifty times. After the Tasleem statement, the famous Tasbeeh al-Zahra litany is done. Thereafter, the following doxology (zikr) is said:\nسُبْحَانَ ذِيْ الْعِزِّ الشَّامِخِ الْمُنِيْفِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL I'ZZIL SHAAMEKHIL MONEEFE \nGlory be to the Lord of Honor and Sublime Authority.\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْجَلَالِ الْبَاذِخِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANA ZIL JALAALIL BAAZEKHIL A'ZEEME \nGlory be to the Lord of Majesty and Exalted Greatness.\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْمُلْكِ الْفَاخِرِ الْقَدِيْمِ \nSUBHAANA ZIL MULKIL FAAKHERIL QADEEME \nGlory be to the Lord of eternal, splendid sovereignty.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَرٰى اَثَرَ النَّمْلَةِ فِيْ الصَّفَا \nSUBHAANA MAN YARAA ASARAN NAMLATE FIS SAFAA \nGlory be to Him Who makes out the footprints of the ant on the stone.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَرٰى وَقْعَ الطَّيْرِ فِىْ الْهَوَاۤءِ \nSUBHAANA MAN YARAA WAQ-A'T TAYRE FIL HAWAAA-E \nGlory be to Him Who knows the exact time and place of the bird dipping down through the air.\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ هُوَ هٰكَذَا وَ لَا هٰكَذَا غَيْرُهٗ\nSUBHAANA MAN HOWA HAAKAZAA WA LAA HAAKAZAA GHAYROHU.\nGlory be to Him Who is like this and no one other than Him is like this.\nThird: It is recommended to offer a two unit prayer half an hour before midday (zohr). At each unit, Surah al-Faatehah is recited once and Surah al-Tawheed, Ayah al-Kursi, and Surah al-Qadr repeated ten times each.\nFourth: One who fears an oppressor and says the following words on this day will be saved, by Almighty Allah:\nحَسْبِيْ حَسْبِيْ حَسْبِيْ مِنْ سُؤَالِيْ عِلْمُكَ بِحَالِيْ\nHASBEE HASBEE HASBEE MIN SO-AALEE I'LMOKA BEHAALEE.\nSufficient for me, sufficient for me, sufficient for me regarding my asking is Your knowledge of my condition.\nOn this day, Prophet Abraham (a.s.) was born.\nOn this day too, yet according to the narration of the two Shaykhs, Imam Ali Ameer al-Moameneen (a.s.) married Lady Fatimah al-Zahra (a.s.)."
